gprofng: use a POSIX word list for the gp-* compatibility symlinks

install-exec-local writes gprofng's five legacy `gp-*` names as symlinks
onto the current `gprofng-*` binaries, and spells the list with a brace
expansion:

    for i in gp-{archive,collect-app,display-html,display-src,display-text}

Brace expansion is a bash/ksh/zsh extension, not POSIX. make runs recipes
with /bin/sh, so on a system whose sh is dash the loop executes exactly
once with `i` set to the literal, unexpanded string. The result is a
single dangling symlink whose name and target both contain braces:

    gp-{archive,collect-app,display-html,display-src,display-text}
      -> gprofng-{archive,collect-app,display-html,display-src,display-text}

and none of the five intended names. Peios's `sh` role is dash, so it gets
the broken form; distributions whose /bin/sh is bash never see it.

Spelling the list as plain words is POSIX and behaves identically under
bash, so this is portable rather than Peios-specific and is suitable to
send upstream.

Both Makefile.am and Makefile.in are patched: the build consumes
Makefile.in, and .am is kept in step so a regenerated tree does not
reintroduce it.

diff -ur a/gprofng/src/Makefile.am b/gprofng/src/Makefile.am
--- a/gprofng/src/Makefile.am
+++ b/gprofng/src/Makefile.am
@@ -196,7 +196,7 @@
 .PHONY: install-exec-local
 install-exec-local:
 	$(mkinstalldirs) $(DESTDIR)$(bindir)
-	for i in gp-{archive,collect-app,display-html,display-src,display-text}; do \
+	for i in gp-archive gp-collect-app gp-display-html gp-display-src gp-display-text; do \
 		oldname=`echo $$i | sed '$(transform)'`; \
 		rm -f $(DESTDIR)$(bindir)/$$oldname ; \
 		ln -s `echo $$oldname | sed 's&gp-&gprofng-&'` $(DESTDIR)$(bindir)/$$oldname; \
diff -ur a/gprofng/src/Makefile.in b/gprofng/src/Makefile.in
--- a/gprofng/src/Makefile.in
+++ b/gprofng/src/Makefile.in
@@ -1193,7 +1193,7 @@
 .PHONY: install-exec-local
 install-exec-local:
 	$(mkinstalldirs) $(DESTDIR)$(bindir)
-	for i in gp-{archive,collect-app,display-html,display-src,display-text}; do \
+	for i in gp-archive gp-collect-app gp-display-html gp-display-src gp-display-text; do \
 		oldname=`echo $$i | sed '$(transform)'`; \
 		rm -f $(DESTDIR)$(bindir)/$$oldname ; \
 		ln -s `echo $$oldname | sed 's&gp-&gprofng-&'` $(DESTDIR)$(bindir)/$$oldname; \
